**Read:** Revisit the complete sources and calculations used in all three investigations.

Explain the path from identified contamination through chemical state, transport, removal, rinsing, drying and renewed exposure to the useful object. Keep amount, composition, distribution and function distinct. Connect a measurement to the material and region it can actually observe.

**Work:** Defend the residue, rinse and sensitive-manufacturing investigations together. Reproduce a central result independently, revise an assumption after criticism and show the effect on a practical decision. Account for utilities, materials, waste, handling and time rather than stopping at a cleaned coupon.

Continue into facilities, airflow and barriers, qualification and monitoring, specialist production, continuing operation and independent research. The process formation here is part of that wider subject; it does not replace a facility-specific qualified method or complete the remaining manufacturing scope.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).

